Z||000012||rockcrawl||04-24-2001||10:03 PM||||UPS will ship it, just put it in a box and if they ask, tell them it contains auto parts. I've shipped everything from doorskins and fenders, seats and headliners, to transmisions. So far they have never refused any pakage. From my experience their insurance isn't worth sh!t unless they loose the package. If the item arrives damaged, they'll just say it was not properly packaged. <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
