Z||000016||TheFiero64||04-27-2001||03:52 PM||||UPS will take everything up to the size of a ford 9 inch rearend. They asked because they didn't want your package damaged in shipment. If you do send something like fiberglass it should be packed in a BIG box with a lot of stuffing on all sides. I would just say a car part at the counter. I work for UPS and we try to keep damages out of our system.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||10
Z||000017||ferrari_momo||04-27-2001||05:13 PM||||Josh,<BR>i shipped a set of GT tail lights 3 weeks ago to a guy.  He said the package / stuff inside were broken in pieces.  I had to sene him another set.  i filed a claim w/ UPS.  so far, no news yet.  Hope i get pay for them.  I would hate to lose out on the money.  anyway, last week i tired sending scoops.  i also wanted to insured up to 200 bucks.  the lady told me that they will not take any fiberglass parts over 8X10".  that was the story.  hope i never run into her agian. <BR>pat<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
